While creating (and probably maintaining) actual lessons would definitely be
out of the question as far as I'm concerned, it might be more probably to
(with permission of course) put the sound files from the Parallel lessons
onto a CD in the correct order, probably grouping the different lessons (or
more likely subdivisions thereof) into separate tracks for better repetitive
listening. However, I don't know if it would actually benefit learning
enough to justify the effort. In any case, that effort would be
significantly less than composing actual lessons, so it might be worth
looking into.

